nodecode-postkitty is a rewrite of mertkayacs's mertkayacs/postkitty:

  https://github.com/mertkayacs/postkitty
  commit 490d8f992387b610c3b6f32cd87d800dc58c8010
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Mert Kaya (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the five tools (postkitty_scan, postkitty_copy, postkitty_make,
postkitty_redo, postkitty_check) and their answers; the platform and target
table, with the limits and their enforcement the original carried in
data/platforms.yaml; the copy counting rules (X weighted characters after
twitter-text, graphemes, UTF-16 units, UTF-8 bytes, hashtag and mention
caps) and the numbered thread split; the job folder layout, with
text-units, copy files per platform, ready/<platform>/ for passing files and
manifest bookkeeping. Left out, because they needed OpenCV, NumPy, Pillow or
Python's regex engine, or belonged to the Hermes desktop: YuNet face
detection and speaker tracking, so the split, speaker and seam layouts and
the person:N focus are gone and framing is crop or pad; the ONNX model
download and its cache; per-platform repair of a failing file (a failing
render is reported, not rewritten); the contact sheet and the
preview_directive line; and the X weighted count's bare-domain rule, which
now counts only http, https and www links as 23. Rendering is ffmpeg and
probing is the file's own header plus ffprobe, so no Python package is
needed. The skill became (help :postkitty) and the /postkitty command.
